# Development Cycle & File Management

## The 7-Phase Cycle

Every feature follows this mandatory flow. Full details: `docs/ai-context/WORKFLOW.md`

```
Phase 1: PRD Drafting        → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-1-prd-generator.md
Phase 2: Readiness Scoring   → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-2-readiness-scorer.md
Phase 3: Task Generation     → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-3-task-generator.md
Phase 4: Implementation      → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-4-implementation.md
Phase 4 start                → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-4-implementation-bootstrap.md
Phase 5: Testing             → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-5-testing.md
Phase 6: Final Auditing      → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-6-final-auditing.md
Phase 7: Learning            → docs/ai-context/prompts/phase-7-learning.md
Orchestration (Phases 4–7)   → docs/ai-context/prompts/orchestration-runner.md + pnpm prd:autorun
```

Phases 1–3 are human-gated. Phases 4–7 + local merge run autonomously via `scripts/prd-autorun.mjs` (never pushes).

## Directory Structure

```
_prds/wip/       → Active PRDs
_prds/completed/ → Done PRDs

_readiness/wip/       → Active readiness reports
_readiness/completed/ → Done readiness reports

_tasks/wip/       → Active tasks
_tasks/completed/ → Done tasks

_docs/wip/       → Active summaries
_docs/completed/ → Done summaries

_state/prds.json      → Generated PRD lifecycle SSOT (query with `pnpm state:prd -- PRD-XXX` / `pnpm state:index`; do not read full file normally)
_state/locks/*.json   → Runtime agent locks (ignored by git)
_state/schema/*.json  → State and lock contracts
_state/acceptances.json → Operator acceptance store (PRD ≥ 248)
```

## File Naming (Consistent Numbering)

All related files use the SAME 3-digit number and kebab-case name:

```
prd-XXX-{short-name}.md
readiness-XXX-{short-name}.md
tasks-XXX-{short-name}.md
summary-XXX-{short-name}.md
```

Find highest XXX across `wip/` and `completed/`, then +1.

## Gate Contract (PRD ≥ 248)

New PRDs must include:

- `Autonomous Close: eligible | operator-gated`
- Per-FR §11 **Verification Commands** (one runnable command per FR)
- `## Durable Artifacts` section

Enforced by `pnpm verify:prd-ready`.

## Status Values

PRD: Draft → In Review → Approved → In Progress → Code Complete → Operator Verification → Ship Verified → Archived
Task: Not Started → In Progress → Code Complete → Operator Verification → Ship Verified

`[x]` means completed as written. Operator-owned verification remains unchecked and is tracked in `Operator Handoff`.

## State & Lock Rules

- Run `pnpm state:sync` after changing PRD/readiness/task/summary lifecycle data.
- Run `pnpm verify:prd-state` before Phase 7 sign-off.
- Run `pnpm verify:prd-ready -- _prds/wip/prd-XXX-{short-name}.md` before Phase 2 PASS.
- Phase 4–6 work must be claimed via `pnpm prd:start PRD-XXX` (lock + worktree + status row) and pass `pnpm verify:agent-locks`; release via `pnpm prd:stop`. If a `verify:*` gate fails for reasons unrelated to your change, STOP and report — do not bypass or hand-edit its expected format.
- `_STATUS.md` is a human board; `_state/prds.json` is the machine-readable lifecycle source. Agents should use compact `state:*` query commands instead of loading the full JSON into context.
